```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>ID Attribute in JavaScript</title>

    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 40px;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            text-align: center;

            /* Two-color background */
            background: linear-gradient(to right, powderblue, lightyellow);
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 700px;
            margin: auto;
            padding: 35px;

            background-color: white;

            border: 3px solid #333;
            border-radius: 20px;

            box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
        }

        h2 {
            color: darkblue;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        p {
            font-size: 18px;
            line-height: 1.6;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }

        #myHeader {
            background-color: tomato;
            color: white;

            padding: 25px;
            margin: 25px 0;

            border-radius: 15px;

            font-weight: bold;

            transition: 0.3s;
        }

        #myHeader:hover {
            background-color: orange;
            color: black;

            transform: scale(1.05);

            cursor: pointer;
        }

        button {
            background-color: darkblue;
            color: white;

            padding: 12px 25px;

            border: none;
            border-radius: 10px;

            font-size: 17px;
            font-weight: bold;

            cursor: pointer;

            transition: 0.3s;
        }

        button:hover {
            background-color: limegreen;
            color: black;

            transform: scale(1.08);
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <div class="container">

        <h2>Using The id Attribute in JavaScript</h2>

        <p>
            JavaScript can access an element with a specified
            <b>id</b> by using the
            <b>getElementById()</b> method:
        </p>

        <h1 id="myHeader">Hello World!</h1>

        <button onclick="displayResult()">
            Change Text
        </button>

    </div>

    <script>
        function displayResult() {
            document.getElementById("myHeader").innerHTML =
                "Have a nice day!";
        }
    </script>

</body>

</html>
```
